  "claim": "The 1995 show \"Mindfreak\" was written by who along with Marcus Monroe was a founding member of The Optical Delusions. The star of the show \"Mindfreak\" generated $150 million in tourist revenue for his live performance show in Paradise, Nevada.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Criss Angel. Sentence: Christopher Nicholas Sarantakos (born December 19, 1967), known by the stage name Criss Angel, is an American magician, illusionist and musician.\nPage: Criss Angel. Sentence: He is known for starring in the television and stage show \"Criss Angel Mindfreak\" and his previous live performance illusion show \"Criss Angel Believe\" in collaboration with \"Cirque du Soleil\" at the Luxor casino in Las Vegas.\nPage: Criss Angel. Sentence: The show generated $150 million in tourist revenue to Las Vegas in 2010, but has since been replaced by \"Mindfreak LIVE\" on 11 May 2016 (the show is partly produced by Cirque, however the directive rights are entirely with Criss Angel).\nPage: Luxor Las Vegas. Sentence: Luxor Las Vegas is a hotel and casino situated on the southern end of the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.\nPage: Ben Seidman. Sentence: His inventions are employed in A&E’s program Mindfreak, starring Criss Angel, where Seidman served as writer and adviser for three seasons.\nPage: Marcus Monroe. Sentence: Monroe, along with Ben Seidman and Luke Jermay is a founding member of The Optical Delusions, a 2008 touring show that billed itself as \"an evening of new-school variety.\"",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Criss Angel. Sentence: Christopher Nicholas Sarantakos (born December 19, 1967), known by the stage name Criss Angel, is an American magician, illusionist and musician.\nPage: Criss Angel. Sentence: He is known for starring in the television and stage show \"Criss Angel Mindfreak\" and his previous live performance illusion show \"Criss Angel Believe\" in collaboration with \"Cirque du Soleil\" at the Luxor casino in Las Vegas.\nPage: Criss Angel. Sentence: The show generated $150 million in tourist revenue to Las Vegas in 2010, but has since been replaced by \"Mindfreak LIVE\" on 11 May 2016 (the show is partly produced by Cirque, however the directive rights are entirely with Criss Angel).\nPage: Luxor Las Vegas. Sentence: Luxor Las Vegas is a hotel and casino situated on the southern end of the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.\nPage: Ben Seidman. Sentence: His inventions are employed in A&E’s program Mindfreak, starring Criss Angel, where Seidman served as writer and adviser for three seasons.\nPage: Marcus Monroe. Sentence: Monroe, along with Ben Seidman and Luke Jermay is a founding member of The Optical Delusions, a 2008 touring show that billed itself as \"an evening of new-school variety.\"",
