        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fb2096a6-b210-5d0f-a870-bf95b741e837",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Criss Angel, Christopher Nicholas Sarantakos, Ben Seidman, Marcus Monroe, Luke Jermay\n- Shows/Projects: Criss Angel Mindfreak, Criss Angel Believe, Mindfreak LIVE, The Optical Delusions\n- Organizations/Companies: Cirque du Soleil, A&E\n- Places: Luxor Las Vegas, Las Vegas Strip, Paradise, Nevada, Las Vegas\n- Roles: magician, illusionist, musician, writer, adviser, founding member\n\nFacts:\n- Christopher Nicholas Sarantakos was born on December 19, 1967, and is known by the stage name Criss Angel.\n- Criss Angel is an American magician, illusionist, and musician.\n- In 2008, Marcus Monroe, Ben Seidman, and Luke Jermay became founding members of The Optical Delusions, a touring show described as \"an evening of new-school variety.\"\n- In 2010, Criss Angel Believe generated $150 million in tourist revenue to Las Vegas.\n- Criss Angel starred in the television and stage show Criss Angel Mindfreak.\n- Ben Seidman served as a writer and adviser for three seasons on A&E's program Mindfreak, which starred Criss Angel, and his inventions were used in the program.\n- Criss Angel Believe was a live performance illusion show by Criss Angel created in collaboration with Cirque du Soleil at the Luxor casino in Las Vegas.\n- On May 11, 2016, Mindfreak LIVE replaced Criss Angel Believe, and although Cirque du Soleil partly produced the show, Criss Angel retained the directive rights.\n- Luxor Las Vegas is a hotel and casino on the southern end of the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "64fd9dd3-cff4-597d-a709-f13c8456a4f9",
        "text": "Page: Criss Angel. Sentence: Christopher Nicholas Sarantakos (born December 19, 1967), known by the stage name Criss Angel, is an American magician, illusionist and musician.\nPage: Criss Angel. Sentence: He is known for starring in the television and stage show \"Criss Angel Mindfreak\" and his previous live performance illusion show \"Criss Angel Believe\" in collaboration with \"Cirque du Soleil\" at the Luxor casino in Las Vegas.\nPage: Criss Angel. Sentence: The show generated $150 million in tourist revenue to Las Vegas in 2010, but has since been replaced by \"Mindfreak LIVE\" on 11 May 2016 (the show is partly produced by Cirque, however the directive rights are entirely with Criss Angel).\nPage: Luxor Las Vegas. Sentence: Luxor Las Vegas is a hotel and casino situated on the southern end of the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.\nPage: Ben Seidman. Sentence: His inventions are employed in A&E’s program Mindfreak, starring Criss Angel, where Seidman served as writer and adviser for three seasons.\nPage: Marcus Monroe. Sentence: Monroe, along with Ben Seidman and Luke Jermay is a founding member of The Optical Delusions, a 2008 touring show that billed itself as \"an evening of new-school variety.\"",
